abstract: >-
  Evolution by Emergence is an open research corpus and machine-auditable
  candidate architecture for resource-constrained cumulative evolution.
  Version v22.6 keeps everything in v22.5: CORE.md follows one model of
  learning, read as a network, in eight steps, and
  formalization/ebe-core/EbECore.lean audits 91 machine-checked results. It
  adds an account of identity as the imprint of a learning path: a position,
  which is both what a learner brings and what it cannot see from there, and a
  path it chooses onward. The question "Where, when, why and from whom did you
  learn that?" gives a view its context, time, function and source, so that
  one view can be checked or revised without an attack on the whole person,
  and a category dissolves into a particular history; its "from whom" meets
  "keep alive what keeps you alive". A concept note gives a practice anyone
  can follow, with worked examples. A new core-Lean module, LearnedIdentity,
  checks 13 results, and the Discovarian creed gains the line "Ask where it
  was learned". Retained from v22.5: TamedCapture, duties to the quality of a
  relationship, a shared identity as learners, and a separate section on
  transparent pricing with its own 76-result core-Lean package.
  DIALOGUE.md records how the author and an AI assistant build the model
  together, now in 31 entries. The release title uses "simulation of reality"
  to mean the internal model through which a system experiences and acts in
  the world, not a claim that reality itself is simulated. Formal verification
  establishes implications under explicit premises; empirical, causal,
  political and normative interpretations remain open.
